":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether all the degrees should be in a bracket."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"font","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"halign","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different. The most typical case is for credits, such as:"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"valign","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the text. Defaults are implementation-dependent."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLHarmonyV5ChordV4KindV5value11usesSymbols4text17areDegreesStacked0jK13InParentheses0jK9Bracketed8position4font5color6halign6valignA2G5ValueO_SbSgSSSgA3uA11MXLPositionVAA7MXLFontVAA8MXLColorVSgAA18MXLLeftCenterRightOSgAA9MXLValignOSgtcfc","roleHeading":"Initializer","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"init(value:usesSymbols:text:areDegreesStacked:areDegreesInParentheses:areDegrees